WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.800
If you want to hear the unknown origins and
abilities of the Other Mother that we don’t

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.759
see in the story, then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.600
This lesson is sponsored by Audible.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.200
[INTRO]

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.640
The Beldam is the dreaded seamstress that
inhabits a realm used for luring in unsuspecting

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.500
children to feast on their souls.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.150
Welcome to Horror History, last episode we
talked about the history of Coraline Jones,

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.050
so today’s I’ll be covering her antagonist,
The Other Mother, also known as The Beldam.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.880
The story keeps the Beldam mostly shrouded
in mystery, but it does leave little clues

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.820
that we can use to learn more about the creature’s
past, it’s distinctive capabilities and

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.809
moreover its purpose in the twisted world
it calls home.

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:39.879
So who is The Beldam and how did it come to
be?

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:43.480
In order to understand, let’s take it back
hundreds of years to the origin of the Other

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.240
Mother.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.800
[HORROR HISTORY]

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.359
It’s never explicitly stated how old The
Beldam is, but we can determine that by studying

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:54.359
the souls of the victims she has captured.

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:58.039
It seems she has been luring in children for
hundreds of years if not more.

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:01.550
Perhaps her oldest victim is a little boy
whose ghost is discovered by Coraline when

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:02.639
she’s locked behind the mirror.

00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:06.890
When he first sees Coraline he asks, “Art
thou—art thou alive?"

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.979
The phrase is derived from Old English, and
it’s usage started to decline in the 17th

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:11.979
Century.

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:14.770
When Coraline asks if he’s a boy or a girl,
he can’t remember, but he says he used to

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.189
wear skirts, but believes he was a boy.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:20.890
He may be speaking of a style called breeching
where boys younger than eight would be dressed

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.909
in articles of clothing known as breeches,
and that practice was most common from the

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:27.150
1500s to the early late 1800s.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:31.960
I researched the year by year usage of some
of the other words the boy uses, like Governess,

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.810
Tain’t, Scullery and Peradventure and determined
that the boy most likely lived between 1700

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.009
and 1760.

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:41.950
It is possible that the Beldam is older than
that, but the boy is her first known victim.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:46.289
The word Beldam as we know it today actually
goes back to the 1660s, and refers to an old

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:50.270
woman or witch, a possible clue about the
nature of the Beldam’s powers having something

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.520
to do with witchcraft.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.369
The stone that Miss Spink and Miss Forcible
give Coraline to help combat the danger that

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:59.149
she might encounter is an Adder Stone, which
is also known as a Hag Stone or Witch Stone.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:03.340
Coraline uses it’s magic to find the souls
hidden by the Beldam, so it makes sense that

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.039
a witch artifact would need to be used to
combat against a witch.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:09.290
Additionally, the Adder Stone is said to be
made from the head of a serpent, the word

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:11.500
“adder” actually refers to a type of snake.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.440
The Beldam has many spider-like properties,
and including the final form we see being

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.660
and arachnid creature, and spiders are said
to be afraid of snakes.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.300
At least that’s what Harry Potter taught
me.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.620
"It is an ancient creature we spiders fear above all others."

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:30.520
Witches are often portrayed with the ability
to transform into an animal form, so it makes

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.940
sense that The Other Mother’s true form
is a spider.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.470
It seems that the Beldam has the ability to
take almost any form it wants, so it’s possible

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.600
that it only took the spider form at the end
because Coraline is afraid of spiders, however,

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.220
some of her more intrinsic attributes
point to her true form being a spider, which

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.240
I will point out as we go through her story.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.460
For example, the Beldam has been living in
this other world for 100s of years and using

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.012
it to lure in kids so she can steal their
souls, which is at one point compared to how

00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:55.430
a spider weaves its web to capture flies.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.850
It’s never explicitly stated why she needs
these kids’ souls, but according to The

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:03.300
Cat, "She wants something to love... I think

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.760
Something that isn't her.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.290
She might want something to eat as well.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.070
It's hard to tell with creatures like that."

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.660
So it seems like she needs to lure in these
children so that she can eat them, or possibly

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.880
capture their souls and slowly feast off them
for 100s of years.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.520
At the time Coraline’s family moves into
the house, the Beldam has captured at least

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.870
three of these souls.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.520
Her world seems to be anchored to this one
particular house, because all of her victims

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.921
seem to be kids who lived there; she doesn’t
seem to have the ability and travel to seek

00:03:27.921 --> 00:03:31.540
out new victims, which may explain why she’s
so desperate to capture Coraline.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.930
She also has the ability to manipulate her
world to make it more attractive to the kid

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.140
that she’s trying to abduct.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.730
When Coraline moves in, she gets to work creating
the perfect world so that Coraline will want

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.770
to stay there forever.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:44.410
She seems to be able to fabricate her own
realities, but “she couldn’t truly make

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.240
anything,” she only had the ability to “copy
and distort things that already existed.”

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.230
So she spends two weeks studying Coraline’s
behaviour and building a world that consisted

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.150
of three wonders designed to entice the young
girl, like a theater that performs amazing

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.250
and thrilling displays to counter the boring
old ladies downstairs, a spectacular mouse

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.320
circus in place of the strange man living
above the Joneses, and home with delicious

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.600
food and attentive parents as opposed to Coraline’s
real home, where he parents are always busy

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.890
and the meals rarely cater to her palette.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.320
The Beldam built a gateway between the two
pockets of reality behind a blocked off doorway

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.710
to another flat that had piqued Coraline’s
interest upon discovering it.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:22.040
There were other ways in and out of the world,
which are used by The Cat, but we never end

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.210
up seeing any of them.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.970
When the illusion is ready, The Beldam uses
her magic to invade Coraline’s dream, making

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.540
her see dark shapes that gather under the
moon and sing, probably to make her dreams

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.760
seem more interesting than her reality and
make her appreciate the other world even more.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.390
One day Coraline’s curiosity gets the better
of her and she swipes the key to the unused

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:42.200
door and opens it to find the passageway,
on the other side of which she meets her Other

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.200
Mother.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.990
She is described as being taller and thinner
than her real mother, which paper-white skin,

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.210
longer teeth, shiny black hair that drifts
as if blowing in a wind or a current and large

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.910
black buttons in place of her eyes.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.880
She tells Coraline to go get her Other Father,
who is another creation of the Beldam.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.790
It does seems that there are other life forms
in the other world, but they are completely

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.790
at the mercy and control of the Other Mother.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:05.540
The Other Father is the first example, but
he doesn’t have the same origin as The Other

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.540
Mother.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.040
It seems he’s more of a featureless blank
slate life form that she has formed and manipulated

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.670
to look and act like Coraline’s father,
and she’s given him black button eyes to

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.380
sell the idea that the two of them are a couple,
just like Coraline’s real parents.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.080
The fact that The Other Mother sews together
these creations is another example of her

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:25.300
similarity to spiders, who weave webs using
string, which they also use to wrap up their

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.000
victims.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.920
The Beldam is the only life form of her kind
in the other world, but there are two other

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:34.140
entities lurking in the dark whose origins
have never been fully elaborated on until

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:34.940
now.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:43.410
If you want to fully experience the dark twisted
world of Coraline, the best way to do it is

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.680
by listening to the audiobook on Audible.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.980
The audiobook is narrated by Coraline’s
legendary author, Neil Gaiman.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:52.660
I love listening to the story and knowing
that every line is being told exactly the

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:53.890
way the author intended it.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:57.390
But I use Audible for so much more than just
diving deeper into Coraline.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.760
Pretty much any book you can think of has
a narrated version on Audible, but that’s

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.490
far from the extent of their offerings -- you
can also listen to podcasts, comedy performances,

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:08.930
Audible originals that you’ll never find
in print and so much more.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.260
What I love about the service is that it can
be so hard to find the time to read a book

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.810
in today’s world, but thanks to Audible,
you don’t really have to.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.540
It’s great for me when I’m making these
videos because I don’t have to stop every

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:21.100
time I want to take notes, I can just have
it continue reading while I'm typing.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.880
And when I’m listening to a title for fun,
I can turn it on in the car, while I’m cooking,

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.500
while I’m exercising, sometimes even while
I’m working and I get to hear so many great

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.930
stories that I never would have had the time
for before.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.889
Just visit audible dot com slash czsworld
or text czsworld to 500-500.

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.830
I’ll leave the link for you in the description.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.740
Again, that’s audible dot com slash czsworld.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.580
The Other Mother and Other Father tell Coraline
that everyone has a second set of parents,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.791
and this is all part of the lie created by
The Other Mother to make Coraline feel more

00:06:50.791 --> 00:06:52.250
comfortable staying in the other world.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.800
She sends Coraline up to play with the rats
in her bedroom.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:57.889
The rats are basically like henchman that
do all of Other Mother’s bidding.

00:06:57.889 --> 00:07:01.750
They entertain Coraline and stack on top of
one another to give a humanoid form to the

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:02.850
clothes of the man upstairs.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:06.960
At first she thinks that this is simply The
Other Mr. Bobo, just as she has an Other Mother

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.620
and Other Father, but by the end of the book
it becomes clear that The Other Mother doesn’t

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.920
have someone to play that role, it’s actually
just the group of mice pretending to be a

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:14.500
person.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.800
But there are two more human-looking “other”
forms that Coraline encounters in the Beldam’s

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.870
world, which she encounters when she goes
downstairs to check out the theater that has

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.620
replaced the flat of Miss Spink and Miss Forcible.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.570
Coraline learns that the performers did not
actually look like the old ladies when they

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.510
take off the fat suits and reveal thin young
women with black button eyes.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:35.130
These would be the last two human characters
with buttons sewn over their eyes.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:39.160
So we have the Other Mother, who is the shape-shifting
Beldam herself, the Other Father, who

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.360
doesn’t actually look like Coraline’s
father, and these two women, who are actually

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.150
just wearing costumes to make them look like
Spink and Forcible.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.330
So who are these other life forms living in
The Beldam’s domain?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:51.710
We know that the Other Mother’s goal is
to eventually sew buttons over Coraline’s

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:55.610
eyes, so what if these other people being
manipulated by her the bodies of the children

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.199
she abducted over the years?

00:07:57.199 --> 00:08:01.240
The idea makes sense, because there are only
three of them, two female and one male, and

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.710
we later find that the kids’ souls have
been removed from their bodies, and they continue

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.729
to exist only as ghosts who can no longer
remember what they were like in life.

00:08:08.729 --> 00:08:11.860
While Coraline is busy inside the theater,
The Other Mother returns to the real world

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.600
and kidnaps Coraline’s parents.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.120
She imprisons them inside of a snowglobe and
hides it away on the mantle in the drawing

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.320
room of the other world.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.640
At the end of Coraline’s visit to the theater,
her other parents greet her outside of the

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.680
house and make the offer to let Coraline stay
forever if she can sew the buttons over her

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:26.680
eyes.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.840
Coraline promptly tells her she’ll be leaving
now, and “her Other Mother’s hand scuttled

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.180
off Coraline’s shoulder like a frightened
spider.”

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.269
They tell her to come back soon, and she leaves.

00:08:34.269 --> 00:08:37.680
The Other Mother seals back up the doorway,
likely to let Coraline’s anticipation of

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.669
returning to the world build before she reopens
it.

00:08:40.669 --> 00:08:43.919
Eventually Coraline returns to the Beldam’s
world to try to find her parents and The Other

00:08:43.919 --> 00:08:47.370
Mother tells her that her parents were bored
of her, and it is here that we learn of another

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:50.949
magic ability she possesses for the purposes
of deceit and manipulation.

00:08:50.949 --> 00:08:54.540
She’s able to brush her hand against the
mirror and create an image of Coraline’s

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.540
real parents.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.579
They appear to be going on vacation without
their daughter and boasting about how nice

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:00.660
it is not to have Coraline weighing them down.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.319
Coraline doesn’t fall for the false image,
so the Other Mother resorts to a less psychological

00:09:04.319 --> 00:09:08.180
tactic by having one of her rats run into
the real world and steal the key to the doorway

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.050
so that Coraline can’t get back out.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.410
The other parents go to bed, commenting on
how they’ll need their beauty sleep if they

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.610
aren’t going to have a midnight snack.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.089
I’m guessing that snack was supposed to
be Coraline, and this is the first suggestion

00:09:18.089 --> 00:09:22.029
of the idea that The Other Mother needs to
eat in order to keep using her powers or spells.

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:25.571
There’s some evidence of this the next day,
then Coraline wakes up and goes into the Other

00:09:25.571 --> 00:09:28.899
Father’s study, and he’s just sitting
there not doing anything at all.

00:09:28.899 --> 00:09:32.009
She also thinks “he looked less like her
true father today.

00:09:32.009 --> 00:09:36.870
There was something slightly vague about his
face—like bread dough that had begun to

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:40.089
rise, smoothing out the bumps and cracks and
depressions.”

00:09:40.089 --> 00:09:43.670
The Other Mother is out in the garden during
this time, working on patching up the other

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:47.100
passageways that exist between the real world
and the other world so that The Cat could

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.740
not freely travel in and out.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:51.189
The Other Mother does not like the cat and
sees him as vermin.

00:09:51.189 --> 00:09:54.850
I think this is because she is afraid of him
and his wit, and going back to idea that her

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:58.809
true form is a spider, cats eat spiders, so
it makes sense that she’d want to keep him

00:09:58.809 --> 00:09:59.809
out.

00:09:59.809 --> 00:10:02.290
The Cat claims there are passages that the
Other Mother doesn’t know about.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.829
Other Mother next encounters Coraline as she’s
returning from a walk and offers to play a

00:10:05.829 --> 00:10:08.779
game, which reveals another important trait
of hers, her love of games.

00:10:08.779 --> 00:10:13.069
It is likely that she loves games because
her primary targets seem to all be children.

00:10:13.069 --> 00:10:16.209
It seems she could have easily sewn buttons
over the eyes of Coraline’s parents, but

00:10:16.209 --> 00:10:19.689
elects not to, probably because they have
no nutritional value to her.

00:10:19.689 --> 00:10:23.610
She’s also a notorious manipulator, so games
are an excellent way for her to strike deals

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:26.110
with her victims and cheat her way into winning
them.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:30.230
Coraline doesn’t fall for the idea of playing
a game on The Other Mother’s terms, so The Other Mother

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.560
tries to convince her stay again, casually
eating beetles as she does so.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.640
"They're cocoa beetles from Zanzibar!"

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.500
This is the only thing we actually see the
Other Mother eating during the novella.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:46.730
She doesn’t eat any of the real food that
she prepares for Coraline, and it represents

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.709
the metaphor of how she wants to consume Coraline’s
soul.

00:10:48.709 --> 00:10:52.059
And the Beldam
needs that soul to continue to thrive.

00:10:52.059 --> 00:10:55.429
Unable to get anywhere with Coraline, she
gets upset and claims Coraline has lost her

00:10:55.429 --> 00:10:59.119
manners by refusing to cave into her demands
and locks her in the area behind the mirror

00:10:59.119 --> 00:11:01.809
as punishment and keeps her there until the
following morning.

00:11:01.809 --> 00:11:05.310
During this time, Coraline meets the ghost
children, which teaches us more about what happens

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.699
when The Beldam takes your soul.

00:11:06.699 --> 00:11:09.980
The victims have forgotten their own names
and identities; they are only able to remember

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:13.930
trivial details about their lives and the
feeling of The Other Mother taking their lives,

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:16.089
their joy and their hearts and leaving them
hollow.

00:11:16.089 --> 00:11:19.670
While Coraline is locked away, The Other Mother
scolds the creature she had created to play

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.329
the role of The Other Father for telling Coraline
too much.

00:11:22.329 --> 00:11:25.791
She strips him of any remaining identifying
features and discards him in the dark in the

00:11:25.791 --> 00:11:28.080
cellar below the abandoned flat next door.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.029
She locks him in there and swallows the key.

00:11:30.029 --> 00:11:33.220
The next morning she retrieves Coraline and
brings her to the kitchen table for breakfast,

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:36.560
hoping today would be the day that she finally
breaks her, but Coraline would surprise her

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.749
with a challenge in a scene that teaches us
yet another secret about the true nature of

00:11:40.749 --> 00:11:41.680
the Beldam.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.400
Coraline challenges The Other Mother to a
game of hide and seek.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:54.309
If she can locate the souls of the dead children
and her parents, the Other Mother is to let

00:11:54.309 --> 00:11:55.679
her leave this world.

00:11:55.679 --> 00:11:59.069
Other Mother never planned on keeping her
word even though she swears on her mother’s

00:11:59.069 --> 00:12:00.209
grave to go through with it.

00:12:00.209 --> 00:12:03.730
We don’t know if a creature like The Beldam
actually has parents of it’s own, or a grave

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.069
though, so this could be relatively meaningless.

00:12:06.069 --> 00:12:09.300
Coraline seems privy to that fact, so she
also swears on her right hand.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.779
I think this is a strategic move by The Other
Mother.

00:12:11.779 --> 00:12:14.860
There are many references to her spider like
hands throughout the story,

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:17.569
Her hand is caught
in the closing door, causing it to break off

00:12:17.569 --> 00:12:20.550
of the arm, and it continues to crawl around
with a mind of its own.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.959
What if the Beldam is actually just this hand?

00:12:22.959 --> 00:12:26.800
We know that she has the ability to create
false worlds and and false people, so it’s

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:31.089
possible that the arms, torso, legs, neck
and head were all just for show to give Coraline

00:12:31.089 --> 00:12:32.449
a false sense of security.

00:12:32.449 --> 00:12:35.679
So she had no issue betting on her mother’s
grave because she likely doesn’t have a

00:12:35.679 --> 00:12:38.940
mother and no issue betting on her right hand,
because that would really just be freeing

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.230
her from the rest of her body.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:44.160
After making the deal, The Other Mother disappears
until Coraline has found two of the three

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.660
souls of the lost children.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:49.249
With each soul found, the world flattens,
loses its form and contorts.

00:12:49.249 --> 00:12:52.149
The once bustling theater becomes abandoned
and derelict.

00:12:52.149 --> 00:12:56.480
I think that without possession of those souls,
which she slowly feeds off of for power, she’s

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.199
unable to keep up the illusion of the perfect
world she had set up.

00:12:59.199 --> 00:13:02.869
She starts to fear that Coraline will find
all of the souls, and appears again to throw

00:13:02.869 --> 00:13:03.899
her off course.

00:13:03.899 --> 00:13:07.610
She regurgitates the key to the empty flat
and implies that Coraline will need it in

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:11.300
order to find the final soul, which is of
course, a lie, but Coraline goes to investigate

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.300
it anyways.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:15.129
Inside, Coraline comes across a giant dead
spider in the bathtub.

00:13:15.129 --> 00:13:19.051
We don’t have any information on any possible
other members of the Beldam’s species, but

00:13:19.051 --> 00:13:22.720
I have to wonder if this is what happens when
one of them doesn’t get children’s souls

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.720
to feed off of.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.699
In the basement, she encounters the thing
that was once The Other Father and the Other

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.080
Mother seems to be influencing his actions,
trying to get him to hurt Coraline.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.540
"Run, child.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.839
Leave this place.

00:13:34.839 --> 00:13:41.980
She wants me to hurt you, to keep you here
for ever, so that you can never finish the

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.560
game, and she will win.

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:48.509
She is pushing me so hard to hurt you.

00:13:48.509 --> 00:13:50.569
I cannot fight her."

00:13:50.569 --> 00:13:54.550
More nervous than ever, the Other Mother sends
her rat spies to go retrieve the final soul

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.230
from where it's hidden upstairs, but she's
able to retrieve it and confront her back

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.350
in the other drawing room.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:02.720
Other Mother plans to trick Coraline into
forfeiting the soul, but Coraline tells her

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:05.760
she thinks she knows where her parents are
hidden: in the passageway between the two

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:06.260
worlds.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:09.940
Other Mother opens it to show her that she
was wrong which would prove her to be victorious

00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:13.630
and earn her the right to see buttons over
Coraline's eyes, but when she turns back,

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:15.949
The Cat is flying though the air towards her
face.

00:14:15.949 --> 00:14:19.619
It scratches and attacks her just long enough
for Coraline to slip through into the passage

00:14:19.619 --> 00:14:24.199
The Beldam screams out, "No!" in an inhuman
voice and reaches out to stop the closing

00:14:24.199 --> 00:14:27.809
door, but it pinches her wrist and servers
her hand, which I theorized could be the real

00:14:27.809 --> 00:14:28.809
form of the Beldam.

00:14:28.809 --> 00:14:32.149
The hand crawls around her Coraline's world
in search of the key so that she would not

00:14:32.149 --> 00:14:35.739
forever be locked out of the other world where
the rest of its body remained.

00:14:35.739 --> 00:14:39.239
That night it was unable to get into Coraline's
room and instead goes downstairs into the

00:14:39.239 --> 00:14:43.449
flat of Miss Spink and Miss Forcible and attacks
one of their dogs, leaving a long gash in

00:14:43.449 --> 00:14:44.449
his side.

00:14:44.449 --> 00:14:47.350
The next day Coraline came to visit the old
ladies and the hand heard her say that she'd

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:51.670
be playing out beyond theold tennis court,
and it realized she have the key with her.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:55.299
To be honest, I'm not sure how it heard what
she said, because last time I checked hands

00:14:55.299 --> 00:14:59.239
don't have ears, but the point is, it secretly
followed her to the spot where it knew she'd

00:14:59.239 --> 00:15:00.239
be alone.

00:15:00.239 --> 00:15:03.959
It arrives to find a tea party with Coraline's
dolls set up on a platform with the key in

00:15:03.959 --> 00:15:04.959
the center.

00:15:04.959 --> 00:15:08.189
When it went to go steal the key, it realized
that the picnic blanket was on no platform

00:15:08.189 --> 00:15:11.800
at all, it was stretched over the top of an
open well, and the hand of the Beldam fell

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.779
into its depths before Coraline sealed the
lid once more.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:18.660
It's unclear if a creature like The Beldam
would be able to survive such a fall, or how

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.860
long it would survive until the next person
comes along and opens the well.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:25.029
It seems reasonable that if it did survive,
it would be able to scale the wall like a

00:15:25.029 --> 00:15:28.670
spider, but it's unlikely that anyone would
open the well again for several years.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:31.139
The Beldam is mysterious but horrifying creature.

00:15:31.139 --> 00:15:34.629
It reminds me a lot of the creature from IT,
from it's shapeshifting abilities, to its

00:15:34.629 --> 00:15:39.470
final form as a spider to its need to feed
off of young children to sustain itself.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:41.759
Another Stephen King connection relates to
The Shining.

00:15:41.759 --> 00:15:45.629
The actress who plays the young version of
the woman in Room 237 is named Lia Beldam,

00:15:45.629 --> 00:15:49.769
and she, similarly to the Beldam in Coraline,
takes a pleasant form to try to win the love

00:15:49.769 --> 00:15:52.470
of her victim before revealing her true nasty
self.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.160
This two-faced personality is yet another
reason that stop motion was the perfect choice

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.949
to make the film version of Coraline.

00:15:57.949 --> 00:16:01.439
The faces of each character had to be replaced
in order give them a variety of expressions,

00:16:01.439 --> 00:16:04.100
and over 15,000 faces were used.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.300
If you want to learn all the secrets hidden
within Coraline, check out the playlist on

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.779
the left, and don't forget to use my link
in the description to listen to the audiobook

00:16:10.779 --> 00:16:15.249
over on Audible. and if you love horror, remember
to subscribe to CZsWorld world for new horrors

00:16:15.249 --> 00:16:16.489
every week, ring that.

00:16:16.489 --> 00:16:20.040
deathbell for notifications, and I'll see you
in the next one.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.160
Assuming we both survive.

